    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "79f1a1b2_a4986d72",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/ptdump.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 306,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-08T16:40:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In practive we iterate only when we expand the list of logs with pages because we don\u0027t have memory. I think it is resonable to keep it like this and improve it later on.",
      "parentUuid": "6ab15801_b6a80383",
      "revId": "27f345ca11f222c3e887ea90fd5364129ddd084d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0a9b284_825c5347",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/ptdump.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 358,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-07T18:25:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIRC, this function can be called several times if we overflow seq_file?\n\nIf that\u0027s the case we could do that heavy call several times for nothing. How about doing it in the open directly? The show would just parse what the hyp has dumped?",
      "revId": "27f345ca11f222c3e887ea90fd5364129ddd084d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "946db0d1_a3774cb7",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/ptdump.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 358,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-08T16:40:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the _show* family of callbacks is invoked whenver the underlying buffer needs to be extended to accomodate the growing logs. That wouldn\u0027t necessarily be correct because you will show the *snapshot* from the open time and not from the moment when you read the sysfs file.",
      "parentUuid": "f0a9b284_825c5347",
      "revId": "27f345ca11f222c3e887ea90fd5364129ddd084d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8af87746_4733dd1f",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/ptdump.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 358,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-09T11:52:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think showing the snapshot from the open time is a problem, there\u0027s no sync mechanism at stake. We don\u0027t keep any lock between the snapshot and the print in a first place, so even doing it during the -\u003eshow wouldn\u0027t assure that what you\u0027ve print is not out of date.\n\nHowever doing it solely in the open would potentially save one (or more!) costly dump!\n\nI have a test where I dump every few seconds the page-table. If I\u0027m unlucky enough and it never fits the first seq_file attempt it means I\u0027ll do twice more dump than necessary won\u0027t it?",
      "parentUuid": "946db0d1_a3774cb7",
      "revId": "27f345ca11f222c3e887ea90fd5364129ddd084d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b920890b_b8195f1f",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/ptdump.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 358,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-09T13:25:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there `is` a problem because you expect userspace to behave in a certain way. Eg. capturing a snapshot at open and reading the file after 2 minutes will show the snapshot from 2 minutes ago.",
      "parentUuid": "8af87746_4733dd1f",
      "revId": "27f345ca11f222c3e887ea90fd5364129ddd084d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e5a7e69_f433e46e",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/ptdump.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 358,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-09T14:12:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I understand your point. IMO that\u0027s debatable what a userspace client can expect here.\n\nBut then if you want to keep the dump in the first show, you could save if `seq_has_overflow()` at the end of the _show() function and to not re-dump if it has overflowed?",
      "parentUuid": "b920890b_b8195f1f",
      "revId": "27f345ca11f222c3e887ea90fd5364129ddd084d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
